# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# A name a held callable requires is asked of the callers of the method
# that calls it, as any hidden input is. r reads zz, which the unit does not
# declare; the definition f calls r and only hands the name on. inner calls
# the held f and has no zz; outer, which calls inner, has zz 30: r reads 30
# and the call gives 5 + 31. direct has zz 40 and calls r itself: 41.
# Entry 7.
fn: r () int
    return: zz + 1
end: r

fn: mk (int: k) fn: () int
    fn: f () int
        return: k + r()
    return: f

@: u0 mk(5)

fn: inner () int
    return: u0()
end: inner

fn: outer () int
    int: zz 30
    return: inner()
end: outer

fn: direct () int
    int: zz 40
    return: r()
end: direct

int: a outer()
int: b direct()
int: ok 7
if: a != 36 || b != 41
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
